Based on the “Show Code” preview pulling in your global FeatureFlags decorator, Storybook is simply dumping the wrapper around your stories instead of the actual Notification JSX. The fix is to tell Storybook’s Docs addon to strip out (exclude) decorators when rendering the code snippet. You can do that by adding a `parameters.docs.source.excludeDecorators: true` block to your CSF file.

Here’s a *SEARCH/REPLACE* patch against  
packages/react/src/components/Notification/next/Notification.stories.js  

```javascript
### packages/react/src/components/Notification/next/Notification.stories.js
<<<<<<< SEARCH
export default {
  title: 'Components/Notifications',
  subscomponents: {
    ActionableNotification,
    InlineNotification,
    ToastNotification,
  },
  decorators: [
    (Story) => (
      <FeatureFlags flags={{ 'enable-v11-release': true }}>
        <Story />
      </FeatureFlags>
    ),
  ],
=======
export default {
  title: 'Components/Notifications',
  parameters: {
    docs: {
      source: {
        excludeDecorators: true,
      },
    },
  },
  subscomponents: {
    ActionableNotification,
    InlineNotification,
    ToastNotification,
  },
  decorators: [
    (Story) => (
      <FeatureFlags flags={{ 'enable-v11-release': true }}>
        <Story />
      </FeatureFlags>
    ),
  ],
>>>>>>> REPLACE
  argTypes: {
    kind: {
      options: [
        'error',
        'info',
        'info-square',
        'success',
        'warning',
        'warning-alt',
      ],
      control: {
        type: 'select',
      },
    },
    className: {
      control: {
        type: 'text',
      },
    },
  },
```

With this change, the “Show code” preview will strip out the wrapper and only show the actual `<InlineNotification …/>`, `<ToastNotification …/>`, or `<ActionableNotification …/>` markup you care about.
